{"acceptance_length": 4.016393442622951, "acceptance_lengths": [6, 2, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4, 5, 3, 1, 4, 2, 2, 1, 3, 11, 1, 7, 4, 1, 6, 3, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 4, 2, 3, 1, 8, 16, 10, 9, 1, 3, 1, 4, 3, 5, 4, 4, 10, 9, 1, 5, 2, 4, 1, 1, 1, 16, 6, 6, 8, 1, 3, 13], "accepted_draft_lengths": [5, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 3, 4, 2, 0, 3, 1, 1, 0, 2, 10, 0, 6, 3, 0, 5, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2, 3, 1, 2, 0, 7, 15, 9, 8, 0, 2, 0, 3, 2, 4, 3, 3, 9, 8, 0, 4, 1, 3, 0, 0, 0, 15, 5, 5, 7, 0, 2, 12], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 3410321408, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 3410316288, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following information:\n\n- John rents his car out **10 times a month**.\n- Each time he rents the car, he gets **3 hours**.\n- He is paid **$25 per hour**.\n- His **car payment** is **$500**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the total hours he gets paid\n\nHe rents the car 10 times, and each time he rents it for 3 hours:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total hours} = 10 \\times 3 = 30 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the total amount he gets paid\n\nHe is paid $25 per hour, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total payment} = 30 \\times 25 = 750 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Subtract the car payment from the total payment to find the profit\n\n$$\n\\text{Profit} = 750 - 500 = \\boxed{250} \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{250}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 1.5924520143307745, "draft_calls": 61, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 76, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "5254f2a3fa288266fa1e4154ba29eb85e6f90b5ff9c907974b1f0b222a198b6e", "method": "relay_reduced", "output_hash": "a500db5221f31ee2deca4f1c56b274a2cf77e6ef2056e473ddb561db76fb245d", "output_tokens": 244, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 3475367936, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 3565158400, "problem_id": "gsm8k/6dbed0240798dcb4", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 312.26886510849, "prefill_full_target": 20.188127517700195, "prefill_relay": 0.047200001776218414, "relay": 11.95948800444603, "unat